WHAT?!

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.440
Anyway, what I learned the most about was his speed.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.275
You see, Sonic demonstrates a lot of different speeds throughout this trailer.

00:02:40.275 --> 00:02:45.735
At the very beginning, he clocks in at a whopping 760 miles per hour on the Sheriff's dash-mounted radar gun.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.180
Giving credit where credit's due, this is actually a pretty cool easter egg,

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:52.220
since Sonic is known for rolling around at the speed of sound,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.765
and the speed of sound is 767 miles per hour.

00:02:55.765 --> 00:02:58.805
So he is, in this scene, rolling around at the speed of sound.

00:02:58.805 --> 00:03:02.000
So the movie got that fact about Sonic totally right,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.860
and got everything else in this scene totally wrong.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.640
You see, Sonic running past a radar gun like that probably wouldn't return a speed reading at all.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.580
Speed guns shoot radio waves forward,

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.580
which bounce of the target and back at the gun.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.580
Since Sonic is moving away from the gun,

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.220
those bounced back waves would get stretched out.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.420
If Sonic was approaching the gun, those waves would've gotten compressed.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.280
This is called the Doppler Effect, with the gun measuring the change in radio wave frequency,

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.500
and converting that into a final speed.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.780
Here's the thing though - cops aren't dealing with cars traveling at near sonic speeds.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.140
As such, police radar guns tend to cap out at 200 miles per hour,

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:44.020
meaning that Sonic, to their equipment, would probably be invisible.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:47.220
But this scene is just Sonic, and his trailer, getting warmed up.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:51.400
After performing a few stretches, we see Sonic's speed hit whole new levels.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.300
In these two frames, we see Sonic erupting into a massive explosion

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:59.260
that knocks out power for apparently the entirety of North America.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.780
Starting in Mexico, apparently.

