"You're basic."

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:34.780
Dr. Robotnik,

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.580
while Jim Carrey fires off a salvo of rockets from his attack drones.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.300
Now, obviously this whole thing is happening during bullet time,

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:42.900
or, let's say "Sonic-vision",

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:46.100
where time is slowed down to Sonic's perspective of the world.

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:50.795
So, he must be fast, because the rockets are literally standing still.

00:07:50.795 --> 00:07:54.700
And Sonic uses this opportunity to redirect the missiles and bullets away from him,

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.800
and - TOWARDS THE GROUND?!

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.060
SONIC! THERE  ARE PEOPLE DOWN THERE!

00:07:59.060 --> 00:07:59.840
JEEZ!

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.500
You not only look like a monster, but you act like one too!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:06.500
Anyway, to calculate the true speed that he's going in this scene,

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:10.120
I measured his movement against the one thing that's also fast enough

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:13.620
to have perceived motion while in Sonic-vision - explosions.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:19.060
We see here, an explosion happening in slow-motion as Sonic moves from one drone to the next.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.780
So, by researching the speed of that explosion,

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:24.780
and then seeing how fast Sonic is moving relative to that,

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:26.760
we can actually get his true movement speed.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:31.120
Now, we have no way of knowing what kind of explosives that Eggman is using in these missiles,

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.080
but we do know the detonation speed of C-4,

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.495
which is 18,000 miles per hour,

00:08:36.495 --> 00:08:38.825
or 8,050 metres per second.

00:08:38.825 --> 00:08:42.620
So, we can use that as an approximation of what we're seeing here.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.820
Knowing that Sonic is the size of a small child in the movie,

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:47.540
"Do you have your child in that bag?"

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.700
*cringe*

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:51.640
Which coincides with his canon heights,

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:55.520
("heights" plural, because Sonic the Hedgehog has two, of course!)

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.240
that are always around 3 feet,

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:02.780
we can actually estimate the size of each of these drones to be similar to this existing spherical drone,

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:06.260
that's 88 centimetres in diameter, or about 2.8 feet.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.695
It takes 0.5 seconds of Sonic-time for the drone to explode to their diameter,

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:15.840
and in that time, 10 frames of footage, Sonic is able to travel 4 times the diameter of the drone.

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:18.020
So doing a few calculations and proportions,

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:25.900
we're able to conclude that Sonic is moving in this scene at 72,038 miles per hour.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:28.920
(That is 32,204 metres per second)

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:34.740
For reference, the fastest ever spacecraft  was 36,000 miles per hour,

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.560
and Sonic is twice that speed,

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:40.980
with movement that fast, he is on par with some meteors,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.280
which can range from 25,000 to 100,000 miles per hour.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.140
At this point, he is going HYPER fast,

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.220
but hold my chilli dog,

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.535
because I'm not done,

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.220
nor is this trailer.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:54.640
You see, that roadway scene from a while back is a bit misleading.

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:58.460
Sure, I calculated that he's running at 1200 miles per hour,

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:04.820
but he also creates a blast that apparently knocks out the electricity for the entire North American continent.

00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:08.440
It seems like what he's created there should be a sonic boom,

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:11.280
since, you know, he's traveling faster than the speed of sound,

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.540
but THAT is not a sonic boom,

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.620
THIS is a "Sonic Boom"!

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:17.200
*comedic drums*

00:10:17.205 --> 00:10:18.840
Ugh, bad joke is bad...

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.660
No, but in all seriousness,

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:24.715
sonic booms wouldn't create an explosion that results in a nationwide blackout.

00:10:24.715 --> 00:10:28.200
So, is this just movie logic, bad movie science?

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.320
No, actually.

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:31.600
The trailer isn't wrong here,

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:34.000
and the real explanation for what's going on,

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:38.340
actually explains some of the weird design decisions that they made with Sonic.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:43.525
You see, that blast is most likely an E.M.P. - an electromagnetic pulse.

00:10:43.525 --> 00:10:44.740
Now, what does that mean?

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:47.000
Well, from a very basic standpoint,

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:52.260
electromagnetic radiation is everything from radio waves and microwaves to visible light,

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.060
to X-Rays and Gamma Rays,

00:10:54.060 --> 00:11:00.120
our modern society is built on our ability to harness the power of electromagnetic radiation.

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.295
Cell phones, the internet,

00:11:01.295 --> 00:11:03.560
radio communications, medical equipment,

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:07.820
the list of things that electromagnetism has enabled us to do is nearly endless.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:14.440
Now, an E.M.P. is when you send out a lot of E.M. at once, which overwhelms electrical circuits.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.640
Send out enough,

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:20.200
and suddenly you're overloading power grids and causing massive nationwide blackouts.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:25.540
As a result, one of the biggest fears that your politicians talk about these days is the E.M.P. threat;

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:27.040
"Electromagnetic Pulse attack."

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.820
"Electromagnetic Pulse attack."

00:11:28.820 --> 00:11:31.160
"A large scale E.M.P. event in the United States."

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:34.180
where a foreign country would blow up a nuclear warhead in our atmosphere,

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:36.520
surprisingly not doing a whole heck of a lot to us,

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.625
but would release a bunch of Gamma rays into the atmosphere,

00:11:39.625 --> 00:11:41.760
which would knock a bunch of electrons out of their orbits,

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.700
which then get trapped in Earth's magnetic field,

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:46.480
causing a massive electrical imbalance which needs to correct itself,

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:50.440
which gives rise to a continent-sized E.M.P.

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:52.420
According to the Federation of American Scientists;

00:11:52.420 --> 00:12:00.475
"A large device detonated at 400-500km over Kansas would affect all of the continental U.S."

00:12:00.475 --> 00:12:03.635
Long story short; E.M.P. blasts, while harmless to us,

00:12:03.635 --> 00:12:07.760
could be massively damaging to the infrastructure that our society is built on.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:12.880
Across the country, lights, communication systems and the internet would all go down instantaneously,

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:16.735
and we probably wouldn't even understand why for a while.

00:12:16.735 --> 00:12:21.540
It's crazy, and that is in essence what Sonic is doing in this scene,

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:25.915
and what causes the military to panic and hire Jim Carrey to hunt him down.

00:12:25.915 --> 00:12:29.245
Now clearly in this scene, Sonic isn't creating a nuclear blast,

00:12:29.245 --> 00:12:31.995
we see everything intact after he sprints away,

00:12:31.995 --> 00:12:34.445
but the science still works because, you know,

00:12:34.445 --> 00:12:38.240
Sonic has those classic lightning abilities I talked about a little bit earlier.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.540
While it may seem stupid that this movie chose to have Sonic

00:12:41.545 --> 00:12:44.815
constantly crackling with electricity when he gets ready to run,

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.860
it shockingly makes the science of this scene work out.

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:52.840
In essence, that lightning makes Sonic the equivalent of a charged particle,

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:56.780
which, when traveling at high enough speeds, create Gamma rays.

00:12:56.785 --> 00:12:59.455
This is called "Synchrotron Radiation",

00:12:59.455 --> 00:13:05.775
which in this case could potentially lead to the massive electromagnetic pulse that we see in this movie's trailer.

00:13:05.775 --> 00:13:09.045
A pulse that appears to kick off the entire plot of this film.

00:13:09.045 --> 00:13:13.640
So, how fast would a charged particle like Sonic the Hedgehog need to travel

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:18.000
to create the massive amounts of Gamma rays needed to create an E.M.P. blast like this,

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.035
nearly the speed of light,

00:13:19.035 --> 00:13:24.505
just under 670, 616, 629 miles per hour,

00:13:24.505 --> 00:13:26.915
or about 300 million metres per second.

00:13:26.915 --> 00:13:29.795
Does Sonic traveling at near-lightspeed in this scene sound stupid?

00:13:29.795 --> 00:13:33.960
Well, canonically, it is Sonic's correct speed.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:40.280
In "Sonic Adventure 1", Sonic gets the lightspeed dash, which allows him to race towards rings at light speed.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.080
In "Sonic CD", we see him traveling through time,

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:48.100
which, again, is presumably using his relativistic speeds traveling near the speed of light.

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:49.460
And in "Sonic Colours",

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:51.885
he's not so fast that he can outrun a black hole,

00:13:51.885 --> 00:13:54.475
running for about 30 seconds until he gets sucked back in,

00:13:54.475 --> 00:13:58.860
but it confirms that he's running at a magnitude near the speed of light.

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:04.280
Like it or not, this movie is currently one of the only pieces of Sonic media,

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:09.720
where we actually get to see Sonic traveling at the speeds he's supposed to be traveling,

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:12.540
making this, awful design and all,

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:17.125
the single best portrayal of Sonic the Hedgehog ever,

00:14:17.125 --> 00:14:21.580
because it got his defining feature correct; his speed.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.125
Is it stupid? Absolutely!

00:14:23.125 --> 00:14:27.895
But the speeds that he's supposedly traveling are also stupidly fast,

00:14:27.895 --> 00:14:30.935
and we're finally getting to see some of the real-world ramifications

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.120
of what exactly that would entail now.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:37.280
So sure, "Sonic" (2019) may be the new "Sonic 06",

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:40.680
but it is one of the best portrayals of Sonic ever,

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.300
by truly showing us that

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:45.780
"He's the fastest thing alive!"

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:50.280
The only thing that's faster is this movie heading to the bargain bin.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.000
But hey!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.420
That's just a theory!

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.500
A Film Theory!

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:57.235
Aaaaand cut.

